    &\le \exp\left( - \frac{1}{4} \frac{\gamma^2}{2^{10}} \right) = \exp(- \gamma^2 / 2^{12})
\end{align*}
In the last inequality, we used the fact that $(|L_k| -1)(\Delta - 1) / \hat{n} \ge (\gamma \hat{n} / 4 C - 1)(\Delta - 1) / \hat{n} \ge \gamma / 32 C$.



